summary:
  The artwork door forgets which station is playing, so the station's own
  name goes to Deezer and iTunes as if it were a song.

history:
  Dance Wave! sends "Dance Wave!" as the title with no artist. iTunes had an
  album of that name and its palm-tree sleeve went to the popup and to MPRIS
  (bench, 2026-09-23); the second time round it came straight from the cache.
  The door both roads pass before the network has to know the station.

target:
  package/contents/ui/ArtworkEngine.qml

find:
          if (TrackLogic.stationTalk(query, app.currentStation) || !artist) {

replace:
          if (TrackLogic.stationTalk(query, "") || !artist) {

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_artworkengine.qml::test_the_station_name_split_like_a_song_asks_nobody_for_a_cover.
  The plain "Dance Wave!" line no longer kills it: since 2026-11-02 a line
  without an artist is turned away at the same door whatever the station.
  Line-neutral.
